### §2.7 ToolSchema（§4 B9 决定形态）

```go
package core

// ToolSchema is the contract that defines:
//  1. Go-side validated parameter type (used by Tool.Execute's `params any`)
//  2. JSON Schema emitted to LLM (function calling)
//  3. Runtime validation of LLM-returned JSON
//
// The single-source-of-truth question (C9) is decided in §4 (B9 PoC pending).
// Three candidate mechanisms (placeholder until §4):
//   (a) reflect+jsonschema: source-of-truth = Go struct
//   (b) schema-first codegen: source-of-truth = JSON Schema file
//   (c) struct-tag + hand-written validator
type ToolSchema interface {
    // Marshal returns the JSON Schema sent to LLM.
    Marshal() (json.RawMessage, error)
    // Validate checks LLM-returned JSON against schema and decodes into typed value.
    Validate(raw json.RawMessage) (any, error)
}
```

**Status**：waiting B9 PoC（§4）.

